This work builds on SPIN, introduced in:

  Qian et al. (2025). The Tug of War Within: Mitigating the Fairness-Privacy
  Conflicts in Large Language Models. Proceedings of ACL.

and on its released implementation, DEAN:

  https://github.com/AI45Lab/DEAN
  Copyright (c) AI45Lab, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Portions of the identification logic in the step-1 and step-2 notebooks are
reproduced verbatim from DEAN's src/SPIN.py — specifically
get_set_difference_mask and the coupled-index selection built on it — so that
results replicate the released code rather than a reimplementation of it. Those
sections are marked in the notebooks where they appear.

The softSPIN and iterSPIN variants, the control conditions, the clinical case
study and the normalised-HSIC and linear-CKA extensions are original to this
work.

Evaluation data and benchmarks are the property of their respective authors and
are not redistributed here; the notebooks fetch them at runtime.
